The structure here means if both oidValue and value are null, we'll throw a null exception for value rather than for oidValue.  Are we ok with that?  I am personally, just wanted to make sure it was considered.  An alternative is to just do:
```C#
ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrEmpty(oidValue);
ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(value);
```
without the `!!` on `value`.
